if {Lisa.FirstKitchen} == true:
	Lisa: … and those whispers that the Old Pretender will foment another uprising. Mark my words, he’ll be back.
	Bartholomew: Miss Allgood, what does it matter if he returns to stake his claim once more? His senseless little tantrum will be put down and forgotten again a month hence.
	Lisa: It’s Mrs Bennett now, you’d do well to remember.
	Bartholomew: Yes, of course. I do forget. Mrs Bennett.
	Lisa: Aye. And what about Charlie in any case? We ought to watch lest he returns from his gallivanting in France.
	Bartholomew: The Young Pretender? Toothless if you ask me.
	Lisa: Oh good sir, the threat is genuine. You may not even be around to live it. But the young ones? Oh, if a Catholic should seize the throne…
	Bartholomew: Relent Mrs Bennett, we have company. What say you faceless one about these nasty Jacobites then?
	Devin: My mother was a catholic. But I care not a whit for politics. Only for that which I can hunt.
	Lisa: Aye, to business, then.
	set {Lisa.FirstKitchen} = false
